# ${project.name}

The Checkstyle Plugin generates a report on the code style used by the developers.
For more information about Checkstyle, see [https://checkstyle.org/](https://checkstyle.org/).

This version of the plugin uses Checkstyle ${checkstyleVersion} by default.
It requires Java ${javaVersion}.
You can [upgrade the version used at runtime](./examples/upgrading-checkstyle.html).

The plugin can be configured in the project's POM.
This version of the plugin provides two predefined rulesets: [`sun_checks.xml`](https://checkstyle.org/sun_style.html) and [`google_checks.xml`](https://checkstyle.org/google_style.html).
You can also use a custom ruleset in the plugin configuration.

Goals Overview
--------------

The Checkstyle Plugin has three goals:

- [checkstyle:checkstyle](./checkstyle-mojo.html) is a reporting goal that performs Checkstyle analysis and generates a report on violations.
- [checkstyle:checkstyle-aggregate](./checkstyle-aggregate-mojo.html) is a reporting goal that performs Checkstyle analysis and generates an aggregate HTML report on violations in a multi-module reactor build.
- [checkstyle:check](./check-mojo.html) is a goal that performs Checkstyle analysis and outputs violations or a count of violations to the console.
  It can also fail the build.
  You can configure it to re-use an earlier analysis.

Major Version Upgrade to version 3.0.0
--------------------------------------

These two parameters were removed from the plugin configuration:

- `sourceDirectory`: use `sourceDirectories` instead.
- `testSourceDirectory`: use `testSourceDirectories` instead.

Usage
-----

General instructions on how to use the Checkstyle Plugin are on the [usage page](./usage.html).
The examples below describe more specific use cases.

If you still have questions about the plugin's usage, look at the [FAQ](./faq.html).
You can also contact the [user mailing list](./mailing-lists.html).
The posts to the mailing list are archived.
An older thread can contain the answer to your question.
You can also search the [mail archive](./mailing-lists.html).

If you think that the plugin lacks a feature or has a defect, report it in the [issue tracker](https://issues.apache.org/jira/projects/MCHECKSTYLE/).
When you create a new issue, include a comprehensive description of your concern.
For bug fixes, the developers must be able to reproduce your problem.
Attach entire debug logs, POMs, or little demo projects to the issue.
Patches are welcome.

Contributors can check out the project from the [source repository](./scm.html).
They can also find supplementary information in the [guide to helping with Maven](https://maven.apache.org/guides/development/guide-helping.html).

